How would you measure it?  Total CPU time is a bad measure -- most of the
time is spent thinking.  But you can't really measure how long you spent
thinking -- what about the few minutes you spent consulting spoilers or
note sheets between playing sessions, or the time spent asking for help on
RGRN?  You can measure how long the program was open, but what if you go
to dinner and leave it running?  I guess that's not significant enough for
most people to worry about.

It would be neat if it stored this data -- probably checking the system
time at load and save would be good enough for most purposes.  But it's
probably not worth any effort to code it, especially if it would break
savefile compatibility.



